1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,533
This is Sworn's public page.

2
00:00:02,583 --> 00:00:09,767
Everything on it is read live from Moderato, Tempo's testnet, and nothing is signed.

3
00:00:09,817 --> 00:00:14,933
Tempo's own Zone batch verifier ran inside a zero-knowledge VM,

4
00:00:14,983 --> 00:00:21,650
and a contract with the exact signature of Tempo's verifier checked the proof.

5
00:00:21,700 --> 00:00:23,717
Here is that transaction.

6
00:00:23,767 --> 00:00:27,850
It succeeded, and its event carries the Zone,

7
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:32,500
the height and the digest the proof committed to.

8
00:00:32,550 --> 00:00:36,633
The page ran this check when it loaded;

9
00:00:36,683 --> 00:00:42,833
I run it again, live: two read-only calls with the same proof.

10
00:00:42,883 --> 00:00:44,900
The real batch: true.

11
00:00:44,950 --> 00:00:50,583
Change one field, the height, and the proof no longer fits.

12
00:00:50,633 --> 00:00:53,683
The same transaction, on Tempo's explorer.

13
00:00:53,733 --> 00:01:01,950
One limit, up front: this batch comes from Tempo's integration tests, not from a live Zone.

14
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:05,061
The same engine re-runs Tempo's EVM.

15
00:01:05,111 --> 00:01:11,283
A paying agent asks a preflight provider: will the receiver get 500?

16
00:01:11,333 --> 00:01:14,394
This provider is configured to lie.

17
00:01:14,444 --> 00:01:19,580
It answers plus 500, and reserves 500 of its bond.

18
00:01:19,630 --> 00:01:21,135
The agent pays.

19
00:01:21,185 --> 00:01:25,283
The transaction succeeds, but the receiver gets nothing:

20
00:01:25,333 --> 00:01:30,987
its policy blocks this sender, so Tempo's guard holds the 500.

21
00:01:31,037 --> 00:01:38,246
A challenger re-runs that transfer inside a zero-knowledge proof, nine minutes here, sped up.

22
00:01:38,296 --> 00:01:43,950
The contract verifies it, and the bond pays the agent 500.

23
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:47,379
A correct answer can't be slashed.

24
00:01:47,429 --> 00:01:56,521
A challenge against the honest provider verifies the proof, and then reverts: the answer was right.

25
00:01:56,571 --> 00:02:04,521
This question makes a good demo because anyone can check it with a simulation.

26
00:02:04,571 --> 00:02:07,950
The point is the proof underneath.

27
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:09,538
The honest limits.

28
00:02:09,588 --> 00:02:12,185
This is testnet and unaudited.

29
00:02:12,235 --> 00:02:16,421
The Zone batch comes from Tempo's integration tests.

30
00:02:16,471 --> 00:02:21,185
The bond caps what a client can be paid,

31
00:02:21,235 --> 00:02:25,421
and there are no users or revenue yet.

32
00:02:25,471 --> 00:02:32,832
Everything you saw is open source, and the public page re-checks it from chain.

33
00:02:32,882 --> 00:02:34,950
Sworn: Tempo's execution, proven.
